{"name":"Cat’s Eye Marble","hex":"#d6a75d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cat","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Catalan."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Terms relating to animals.\n  A mammal of the family Felidae.","A mammal of the family Felidae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cat"},{"term":"eye","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An organ through which animals see (“perceive surroundings via light”).","The visual sense."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To carefully or appraisingly observe (someone or something).","To consider."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eye"},{"term":"marble","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A metamorphic rock of crystalline limestone. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A small ball used in games, originally of marble but now usually of glass or ceramic."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cause (something to have) the streaked or swirled appearance of certain types of marble, for example by mixing viscous ingredients incompletely, or by applying paint or other colorants unevenly.","To get or have the streaked or swirled appearance of certain types of marble, for example due to the incomplete mixing of viscous ingredients, or the uneven application of paint or other colorants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marble"}],"entries":[{"title":"Marble (toy)","blocks":[{"text":"A marble is a small spherical object often made from glass, clay, steel, plastic, or agate. These toys can be used for a variety of games called marbles, as well being placed in marble runs or races, or created as a form of art. Sizes may vary, but usually range from about 0.5 to 3.5 cm in diameter. They are often collected, both for nostalgia and for their aesthetic colors. In northern England, the game and objects are called \"taws\", with larger marbles being called \"bottle washers\", named after the use of a marble in Codd-neck bottles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Marble_collector_-_Flickr_-_smkybear.jpg/330px-Marble_collector_-_Flickr_-_smkybear.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marble_(toy)","wikidata":"Q200199"},{"title":"Eye","blocks":[{"text":"An eye is a sensory organ that allows an organism to perceive visual information. It detects light and converts it into electro-chemical impulses in neurons (neurones). It is part of an organism's visual system."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Krilleyekils.jpg/330px-Krilleyekils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye","wikidata":"Q7364"},{"title":"Marble","blocks":[{"text":"Marble is a metamorphic rock consisting of carbonate minerals (most commonly calcite (CaCO3) or dolomite (CaMg(CO3)2) that have recrystallized under the influence of heat and pressure. It has a crystalline texture, and is typically not foliated (layered), although there are exceptions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Marmo_z17.JPG/330px-Marmo_z17.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marble","wikidata":"Q40861"},{"title":"Cat","blocks":[{"text":"The cat, also called domestic cat and house cat, is a small domesticated carnivorous mammal. It is a member of Felidae, the family of mammals in the order Carnivora also colloquially referred to as cats. An obligate carnivore requiring a predominantly meat-based diet, it has retractable claws adapted to killing small prey species such as mice and rats. It has a strong, flexible body, quick reflexes, and sharp teeth, and its night vision and sense of smell are well developed. It is a social species, but a solitary hunter and a crepuscular predator.\nCat communication includes meowing, purring, trilling, hissing, growling, grunting, body language, and scent marking. It can hear sounds too faint or too high in frequency for human ears, such as those made by small mammals. It secretes and perceives pheromones. Cat intelligence is evident in its ability to adapt, learn through observation, and solve problems. The domestic cat is the only domesticated species of the family Felidae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Siam_lilacpoint.jpg/330px-Siam_lilacpoint.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cat","wikidata":"Q146"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Kids_playing_%27Kancha%27_Marble_%28toy%29_game_in_Nepal.jpg/500px-Kids_playing_%27Kancha%27_Marble_%28toy%29_game_in_Nepal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Kids_playing_%27Kancha%27_Marble_%28toy%29_game_in_Nepal.jpg/1280px-Kids_playing_%27Kancha%27_Marble_%28toy%29_game_in_Nepal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Kids_playing_%27Kancha%27_Marble_%28toy%29_game_in_Nepal.jpg/500px-Kids_playing_%27Kancha%27_Marble_%28toy%29_game_in_Nepal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Children playing the game 'kancha' near Shambhunath Temple, Nepal","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKids_playing_'Kancha'_Marble_(toy)_game_in_Nepal.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Jeu_de_noix.jpg/500px-Jeu_de_noix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Jeu_de_noix.jpg/1280px-Jeu_de_noix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"htt